message.content:
Sure! Below is a minimal example of an **interactive rotating card** using only HTML and CSS.  
When you hover over the card, it will smoothly rotate around its center.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Container that centers the card */
body {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    height: 100vh;
    background: #f0f2f5;
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    perspective: 800px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
    cursor: pointer;
}

.card-inner {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Preserve 3D children */
    transform-origin: center;         /* Rotate around the center */
}

.card:hover .card-inner {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);        /* Rotate 180° on hover */
}

/* Front side of the card */
.card-front,
.card-back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;     /* Hide backside during rotation */
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    color: white;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 20px;
}

/* Styling for front side */
.card-front {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff7e5f, #feb47b);
}

/* Styling for back side */
.card-back {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #43cea2, #185a9d);
    transform: rotateY(180deg);       /* Start rotated so it's hidden initially */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
        <!-- Front content -->
        <div class="card-front">
            <h2>Front Side</h2>
            <p>Hover over me!</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back content -->
        <div class="card-back">
            <h2>Back Side</h2>
            <p>Thanks for hovering.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **Perspective** – The `.card` container has `perspective: 800px;`.  
   This gives the 3D effect when the inner element rotates.

2. **Transform style** – `.card-inner` uses `transform-style: preserve-3d;` so its child elements keep their 3D positioning.

3. **Rotation** – On hover, we apply `transform: rotateY(180deg);` to `.card-inner`.  
   The back side (`.card-back`) is pre‑rotated by `rotateY(180deg)` so that it becomes visible after the flip.

4. **Backface visibility** – Setting `backface-visibility: hidden;` hides each side when it’s turned away from the viewer.

Feel free to replace the gradient backgrounds, text, or dimensions with your own design. Enjoy the rotating card!
